  Spell of Magic Mapping and spell of Detect Treasure (works the
same as !oObjDet) can do the same jobs.   


  The spell of Clairvoyance can replace Magic Mapping to a 
certain extent.  The ability can also be purchased from Moloch's 
priest in the VotD, as Richard Bos recently pointed out.  (Now 
you know why there's all that gold in Gehennom.)  Wizards can get
clairvoyance from wearing a cornuthaum as well.  

  Carrying Amulet of Yendor also bestows clairvoyance (if you're 
not wearing headgear that blocks clairvoyance).  I guess this is 
why.

  Clairvoyance also works on levels where Magic Mapping is 
blocked.  It probably would work best when combined with teleport
control and the ability to teleport, except on no-teleport 
levels.


  Then you could use the scrolls/potions as you suggest, or you 
could use them as poly fodder.

  That may be why there are so many spellbooks in the VotD, to
give you a last chance at those spellbooks before the mazes in
Gehennom.

  Magic Mapping and Detect Treasure are mostly useful in Gehennom
so polying for the spellbooks seems feasible.  Just be sure to 
finish mapping/detecting Gehennom before 20k turns are up.


  Beings "Skilled" in Divination means Detect Treasure acts 
like a blessed potion of Object Detection:  you can tell exactly
what the top detected objects are.  

  (NB: You only detect the top object in a stack.  You can't 
determine if there are more objects under the top one by any 
remote means that I'm aware of.)


  Even without exact identification Detect Treasure lets you know
where objects aren't, so you can just go to the squares with 
objects.  (By whatever means: teleport, digging, or just walking 
the maze.)


